Pass `prefix`, `tags` and `responses` to the `APIRouter` constructor; every path operation on it inherits them.

```python
from fastapi import APIRouter, FastAPI, HTTPException

router = APIRouter(
    prefix="/items",
    tags=["items"],
    responses={404: {"description": "Not found"}},
)

fake_items = {"plumbus": {"name": "Plumbus"}}

@router.get("/")
def read_items():
    return fake_items

@router.get("/{item_id}")
def read_item(item_id: str):
    if item_id not in fake_items:
        raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail="Item not found")
    return fake_items[item_id]

app = FastAPI()
app.include_router(router)
```

`/items/plumbus` now appears under the "items" group in /docs with the 404 response documented, without repeating those options on each decorator.

Create one router per version with a version prefix and include both; only the endpoints and schemas that change need a v2 copy.

```python
from fastapi import APIRouter, FastAPI
from pydantic import BaseModel

class UserV1(BaseModel):
    name: str

class UserV2(BaseModel):
    first_name: str
    last_name: str

v1 = APIRouter(prefix="/v1", tags=["v1"])
v2 = APIRouter(prefix="/v2", tags=["v2"])

@v1.get("/users/{user_id}")
def get_user_v1(user_id: int) -> UserV1:
    return UserV1(name="Ada Lovelace")

@v2.get("/users/{user_id}")
def get_user_v2(user_id: int) -> UserV2:
    return UserV2(first_name="Ada", last_name="Lovelace")

app = FastAPI()
app.include_router(v1)
app.include_router(v2)
```

Old clients keep calling `/v1` unchanged. Keep business logic in shared functions so the versions differ only in their API layer.

Build each version as a separate `FastAPI` app and mount them under version prefixes; each sub-app generates its own OpenAPI schema and docs.

```python
from fastapi import FastAPI

v1 = FastAPI(title="Shop API", version="1.0")
v2 = FastAPI(title="Shop API", version="2.0")

@v1.get("/products")
def products_v1():
    return [{"name": "Lamp", "price": 10}]

@v2.get("/products")
def products_v2():
    return {"items": [{"name": "Lamp", "price": {"amount": 10, "currency": "EUR"}}]}

app = FastAPI()
app.mount("/v1", v1)
app.mount("/v2", v2)
```

Docs are then at `/v1/docs` and `/v2/docs`. Mounted apps keep their own exception handlers and dependency overrides, and their lifespan doesn't run, so put startup logic on the parent app.

